om/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/deployments","created_at":"2016-10-14T12:27:49Z","updated_at":"2026-10-31T16:52:02Z","pushed_at":"2026-07-24T07:39:04Z","git_url":"git://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:RasaHQ/rasa.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa","homepage":"https://rasa.com/docs/rasa/","size":1707110,"stargazers_count":21364,"watchers_count":21364,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":4914,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":160,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["bot","bot-framework","botkit","bots","chatbot","chatbots","chatbots-framework","conversation-driven-development","conversational-agents","conversational-ai","conversational-bots","machine-learning","machine-learning-library","mitie","natural-language-processing","nlp","nlu","rasa","spacy","wit"],"visibility":"public","forks":4914,"open_issues":160,"watchers":21364,"default_branch":"3.6.x"},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/pulls/11480","html_url":"https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/pull/11480","diff_url":"https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/pull/11480.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/pull/11480.patch","merged_at":"2022-08-26T09:40:28Z"},"body":"**Proposed changes**:\r\n- fixes #11395 \r\n- Also found that an optimization during the copying of `TrackersWithCachedStates` was buggy and in effect turned off. I turned it on again.\r\n\r\n**Terms**\r\nunset slot: a slot that has not been set during conversation. It might have a value though (the initial value)\r\n\r\n**The Problem**\r\nThe situation is as follows: `TrackerWithCachedStates` is being generated with `omit_unset_slots=False` previous to the training of the policies. This way all the initial values are present in the cached states. The issue is, that when the states are requested using `omit_unset_slots=True`, the `TrackerWithCachedStates` just ignored this parameter and returned the cached states that had been created with `omit_unset_slots=False`. \r\n\r\n**Proposed Solution**\r\nThe approach I picked here to solve this is to ignore caching completely and recalculate the states when they are requested with `omit_unset_slots=True`. As far as I could see this is acceptable as the states are only requested with `omit_unset_slots=True` once, namely during the training of the rule policy.\r\n\r\n**Alternative Solutions**\r\n* Potentially, the `TrackerWithCachedStates`, which is only being used during training time, should be generated entirely using `omit_unset_slots=True`. My intuition says that the initial values should probably be omitted for all training aspects. We saw clearly that it breaks the `RulePolicy`. My worry is, that it also breaks the `MemoizationPolicy` and make things more difficult for the ML policies. I think for stories that capture a full conversation, it does not do any damage. However, there are oftentimes stories that are just concerned with 2 or 3 steps in the middle of a conversation. Here the initial value would be integrated into the learning while during the real conversation, the value might be different. Yet it's also difficult to say wether it might be beneficial in some situations... \r\n* We could cache both versions of the states with `True` and `False` for `omit_unset_slots`. However, I think it it would create a lot of duplication of code and as I said only the rule policy requests the data during training once with `omit_unset_slots=True`. All other policies request it with `omit_unset_slots=False`.\r\n* Currently the information about whether a slot with value was set or not is lost the moment a position in the tracker's event stream is transformed into a state. We could change the State data to retain information about the slots being set or unset. Then this information would not be lost and slots could be removed during retrieval of the cached data. Unfortunately, I think this would require big code changes.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Status (please check what you already did)**:\r\n- [x] added some tests for the functionality\r\n- [ ] updated the documentation\r\n- [x] updated the changelog (please check [changelog](https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/tree/main/changelog) for instructions)\r\n- [x] reformat files using `black` (please check [Readme](https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa#code-style) for instructions)\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/issues/11480/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/issues/11480/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":7266214409,"node_id":"CE_lADOBDn5MM5OtnqXzwAAAAGxGaIJ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/issues/events/7266214409","actor":{"login":"twerkmeister","id":1107341,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDczNDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1107341?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/twerkmeister","html_url":"https://github.com/twerkmeister","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twerkmeister/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twerkmeister/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twerkmeister/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twerkmeister/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twerkmeister/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.githu